think Listed the prose lines the Reach reading actually sees. The compass rose's seven numbered stations were among them -- each a dense link-carrying line read as a sentence.
think Read both line rules. measure() and reach_read() each hold out a bullet with /^[ \t]*[-*+][ \t]/ and enumerate no digit, so an ordered-list marker falls through to the body.
think Measured the class before deciding: 1,727 ordered-list lines across 332 of 1,380 living Markdown pages; 207 lines in 38 files across the three gated tiers.
think Patched scratch copies to price the repair. teaching_over_field_target runs 1 to 3 -- docs/CRYPTO.md 30 to 31 percent, the VPN guide 16 to 33 -- so the gate reads ok over two pages standing above their declared target.
think Reach moves both ways: MAP.md 70 to 80, follow-our-compass 50 to 40. No page was graded truly, in either direction.
think qa_report_card.sh refuses twice in its own comments to re-grade the tree in one unmeasured step and names ITINERARY as where the standard question goes. Followed that ruling rather than my own preference.
